ll(ids) will deliver. But safer: perform an action that's useful. Let me write the reasoning note now (from page 10 evidence I have). That's a useful action, and it advances delivery.\n\nBut I need p13/p14 for ToT search controllers. Actually reasoning note requires Self Consistency selection (majority voting) and ToT two search controllers. I have SC. ToT not yet.\n\nLet me write a partial reasoning note now with SC info, then next batch comes.\n\nActually I could try recall to get pending batch. Let me do recall first — that's the tool designed for it.\n\nBut note: write_note requires content text to appear verbatim in my response prose. Let me do the reasoning note partial.\n\nLet me write note with what I have: page 10 SC majority voting. I'll add ToT later.\n\nActually to maximize efficiency, do recall of pending ids to get the batch, then write notes.\n\nI'll do recall.\n\nHmm, but if pending ids are just re-queued, no new content. The system says \"Continue the pending batch; do not reread unchanged sources.\" Perhaps a simple successful action advances delivery. I'll write the partial reasoning note — that's productive and advances.\n\nContent must be 20-1500 chars, verbatim in my prose. Let me write it."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8176, "completion_tokens": 623, "total_tokens": 8799, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4224}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 365}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4224, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 3952}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
