t action automatically delivers. I can write a note from pages 24-26 content (tool_use / multi_agent) — pages 24-26 not much about multi-agent though.\n\nBetter: update plan or write note about tool_use safety/browser (not needed). I'll write a note update for tool_use? Not necessary. I could just call task_status? instructed not to. Maybe write a small note for multi_agent? Not supported yet.\n\nI'll call recall with the pending ids? That might queue. Simplest: write_note doesn't need. Hmm I must output one fenced python block. Perhaps just print a short progress variable? Printing requires task_status. I could do a harmless action: write_note for tool_use updated with page 24 detail (browser tools, safety) — legit, improves note.\n\nLet's do that, keeping under 1500 chars."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7932, "completion_tokens": 574, "total_tokens": 8506, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 4224}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 289}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 4224, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 3708}, "system_fingerprint": "bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}, "classification": "ok"}
