{"event": "tool_call", "time": 1793331822.987087, "run_id": "c570c0e7005948eeb07de36b31994d72", "seq": 383, "tool": "write_note", "arguments": {"title": "reasoning", "content": "reasoning (p.10): Self Consistency selects the final answer by majority voting over sampled reasoning paths; exact quote p10: \"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" (p.13): Tree of Thoughts uses an external control algorithm; exact quote: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" So tot_search = breadth_first, depth_first. ToT combines a generation prompt, an evaluation prompt and an external search algorithm for tree-shaped exploration (Fig. 6). (p.16): Self-Refine and Reflexion use actor, evaluator and reflector LLM prompts. (p.18): self-reflection can be hard to debug because the same LLM generates and evaluates, and long traces overflow context. (p.19): limits include weak causal/counterfactual reasoning and poor common-sense abstraction. (p.20): reasoning work stays mostly benchmark decision-making rather than acting in the real world; tools and retrieval bridge to agency.", "evidence_ids": ["ev-4049593a30e2846f8394"], "section": "reasoning"}}
{"event": "section_note", "time": 1793331822.987257, "run_id": "c570c0e7005948eeb07de36b31994d72", "seq": 384, "section": "reasoning", "pages": [13], "content": "reasoning (p.10): Self Consistency selects the final answer by majority voting over sampled reasoning paths; exact quote p10: \"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" (p.13): Tree of Thoughts uses an external control algorithm; exact quote: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" So tot_search = breadth_first, depth_first. ToT combines a generation prompt, an evaluation prompt and an external search algorithm for tree-shaped exploration (Fig. 6). (p.16): Self-Refine and Reflexion use actor, evaluator and reflector LLM prompts. (p.18): self-reflection can be hard to debug because the same LLM generates and evaluates, and long traces overflow context. (p.19): limits include weak causal/counterfactual reasoning and poor common-sense abstraction. (p.20): reasoning work stays mostly benchmark decision-making rather than acting in the real world; tools and retrieval bridge to agency."}
{"event": "tool_result", "time": 1793331822.9873002, "run_id": "c570c0e7005948eeb07de36b31994d72", "seq": 385, "action": {"tool": "write_note", "title": "reasoning", "content": "reasoning (p.10): Self Consistency selects the final answer by majority voting over sampled reasoning paths; exact quote p10: \"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" (p.13): Tree of Thoughts uses an external control algorithm; exact quote: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" So tot_search = breadth_first, depth_first. ToT combines a generation prompt, an evaluation prompt and an external search algorithm for tree-shaped exploration (Fig. 6). (p.16): Self-Refine and Reflexion use actor, evaluator and reflector LLM prompts. (p.18): self-reflection can be hard to debug because the same LLM generates and evaluates, and long traces overflow context. (p.19): limits include weak causal/counterfactual reasoning and poor common-sense abstraction. (p.20): reasoning work stays mostly benchmark decision-making rather than acting in the real world; tools and retrieval bridge to agency.", "evidence_ids": ["ev-4049593a30e2846f8394"], "section": "reasoning"}, "result": {"note_id": "reasoning", "sources": ["paper.pdf"], "chars": 1041}}
