{"event": "section_note", "time": 1793331828.882328, "run_id": "c570c0e7005948eeb07de36b31994d72", "seq": 397, "section": "outlook", "pages": [51, 52], "content": "outlook (p.51, p.52): Table 4 lists five research-agenda topics: Training Data, Hallucination, Agent Behavior, Self reflection, and Safety. Its challenges include finetuning with inference-time reasoning data, self verification, scalable simulation and role playing, in-model self reflection/metareasoning, and assistant responsibility, privacy and fairness. The conclusion states that the three capability categories build on each other, and p52 says: \"Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.\" Thus the shared foundations are reasoning and self-verification. The agenda emphasizes safety, ethics and trust as major open issues."}
