8f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:47', 'required': True, 'page': 47, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 5018, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-aa9b9dbdfec8c640b495', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:48', 'required': True, 'page': 48, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4375, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-6e64db9ec6bfa8f9417f', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:49', 'required': True, 'page': 49, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4295, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-42cada09d7411017eb46', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:50', 'required': True, 'page': 50, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4663, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:51', 'required': True, 'page': 51, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 3844, 'exposed': True}, {'id': 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3', 'source': 'paper.pdf', 'version': 'b4767423c79db69ae7138f4c0aed7733af6385e0a370da21ad7d6fe029d7fb8c', 'locator': 'page:52', 'required': True, 'page': 52, 'valid': True, 'atomic': True, 'chars': 4072, 'exposed': True}], 'notes': {'overview': {'id': 'overview', 'content': 'overview (p.1,4,5): Agentic LLMs are defined by three capabilities: reason, act, interact. p4 definition: \"Agents that receive input in natural language from their environment, reason to make decisions, and take autonomous actions in affecting their environment, to achieve specific goals.\" p5: \"The categories reasoning–acting–interacting build upon each other\" (virtuous circle, Fig. 1). Literature selection p5: \"The papers were initially selected with a Google Scholar search on Agentic LLM. From there, we used a snowballing approach to discover work that was cited but not yet included in our initial set.\" Also only LLM-based work; related surveys Li 2024, Wang 2024b, Gao 2024, Xi 2023 compared. Limit: survey covers current status only.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-26c94297c50e4ef408a2', 'ev-dbca06e364385e22f3c5'], 'valid': True, 'request': 4}, 'reasoning': {'id': 'reasoning', 'content': 'reasoning (p.10): Self Consistency selects the final answer by majority voting over sampled reasoning paths; exact quote p10: \"Self Consistency is an ensemble approach that samples diverse reasoning paths, evaluates them, and selects the most consistent answer using majority voting.\" (p.13): Tree of Thoughts uses an external control algorithm; exact quote: \"The paper describes both a breadth-first and a depth-first controller.\" So tot_search = breadth_first, depth_first. ToT combines a generation prompt, an evaluation prompt and an external search algorithm for tree-shaped exploration (Fig. 6). (p.16): Self-Refine and Reflexion use actor, evaluator and reflector LLM prompts. (p.18): self-reflection can be hard to debug because the same LLM generates and evaluates, and long traces overflow context. (p.19): limits include weak causal/counterfactual reasoning and poor common-sense abstraction. (p.20): reasoning work stays mostly benchmark decision-making rather than acting in the real world; tools and retrieval bridge to agency.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-4049593a30e2846f8394'], 'valid': True, 'request': 29}, 'tool_use': {'id': 'tool_use', 'content': 'tool_use (p.23-25): Toolformer tests five tools: calculator, question answering system, search engine, translation system, calendar. Quote p23: \"A range of tools is tested: a calculator, a question-answering system, a search engine, a translation system, and a calendar.\" ToolBench: \"ToolBench [Qin et al., 2023] contains 16,464 APIs from RapidAPI\". p24: computer/browser tools (OmniParser, Computer Use, Operator, Browser Use) convert GUI actions into callable tool APIs; agent interoperability protocols MCP, ACP, ANP emerging. p24-25 safety: AgentHarm benchmark with 110 malicious agent tasks; simple universal templates can jailbreak agents; Rainbow Teaming uses quality-diversity (MAP-Elites) to generate adversarial prompts. Limitation: choosing the right tool and integrating results, plus security risk of tool use, remain open.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-4e747765f5046c8ad8b1', 'ev-daeb56e673fc61cae0ef'], 'valid': True, 'request': 13}, 'multi_agent': {'id': 'multi_agent', 'content': 'multi_agent (p.32-37): 三层结构：非agentic LLM社会能力、角色分工的成对/小组agent、无预设角色自组织社会(p32)。4.2.2 CAMEL：两个LLM扮演预定义角色，p37原文：\"By using inception prompting and role descriptions, the agents stay in character and collaborate toward the goal by breaking down complex problems in manageable steps through dialogue.\" 故 camel_prompting = inception_prompting。p37还述creator-critic配对(Constitutional AI)、多agent辩论(Du et al.; MAD含judge)。p35：MAgIC用社交推理游戏与博弈场景评7项能力，GPT-o1与GPT-4显著更好；You.com助手在提议社会行为上优于人类。p35-36：GAMA-Bench、Alympics、AucArena等multi-agent博弈benchmark。Generative Agents的人类评估者人数待p38-39。', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-98a30db9253fff6cc9da', 'ev-a9b70da77a1c104405a2'], 'valid': True, 'request': 17}, 'outlook': {'id': 'outlook', 'content': 'outlook (p.51, p.52): Table 4 lists five research-agenda topics: Training Data, Hallucination, Agent Behavior, Self reflection, and Safety. Its challenges include finetuning with inference-time reasoning data, self verification, scalable simulation and role playing, in-model self reflection/metareasoning, and assistant responsibility, privacy and fairness. The conclusion states that the three capability categories build on each other, and p52 says: \"Robotic interaction and tool-use build on grounded retrieval augmentation, social interaction (such as theory of mind) builds on self reflection, and all categories benefit from reasoning and self-verification.\" Thus the shared foundations are reasoning and self-verification. The agenda emphasizes safety, ethics and trust as major open issues.', 'sources': ['paper.pdf'], 'evidence_ids': ['ev-99f0f0a37d328bfed1a9', 'ev-01ce8948bcc88d235ea3'], 'valid': True, 'request': 30}}}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone", "observations_images": null, "action_output": null, "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 8773, "output_tokens": 456, "total_tokens": 9229}, "is_final_answer": false}}
